# Queue Observation and Prioritization

The queue manager only processes known item types.  
Regularly inspecting the queue for unhandled or unknown items helps inform future automation priorities and backlog planning.

## Why
- Identify unhandled message types early.
- Quantify integration drift or missing automation coverage.
- Use queue metrics to guide what automation capabilities to build next.

## How
- Periodically list or sample queued items.
- Track unknown item types over time.
- Feed insights into backlog refinement and ADR proposals if they suggest design changes.
